(a) Actions by Harris County. Should water or wastes be discharged to the POTW in violation of any provisions of this division, the board may after notifying the offender and providing a hearing before the board:
(1) Terminate water service and/or the discharge of water and wastes by the violator into the POTW;
(2) Require pretreatment into a condition as authorized and/or required by this division, or any water or waters into the POTW;
(3) Require control over the quantities and flow rates of water or wastes entering the POTW as authorized and/or required by this division;
(4) Require payment by the violator to cover the added capital and operating costs, not covered by existing taxes or sewer charges, of handling and treating otherwise prohibited wastes, which can be documented as reasonable charges for the materials, supplies, labor and other costs actually required.
(5) Revoke the user's permit;
(6) Any person failing to pay any sewer charges authorized by this division shall be subject to termination of their sewer service.
Any person who violates any provision of this division shall, upon conviction in the Magistrate Court of Harris County, Georgia, be punished by a fine and/or imprisonment at the discretion of the magistrate.
Further, any industrial user who violates any provisions of section 7-77(h) of this division, shall be subject to a civil or criminal action to be brought by Harris County, and if found to be in violation, civil or criminal penalties up to at least $1,000.00 violation per day may be awarded.
(b) Falsifying information. Any person who knowingly makes any false statements, representation, omission or certification in any application, record, report, plan or other document filed or required to be maintained pursuant to this division or falsify, tamper with, or knowingly render inaccurate any monitoring device or method required under this division or reports of any such monitoring device or method may be subject to a fine or imprisonment under applicable state or federal law.
(Ord. No. 07-14, § 10, 12-16-2014)

